```javascript
function isPalindrome(s) {
    const cleaned = s.replace(/[^0-9a-zA-Z]/g, '').toLowerCase();
    const reversed = cleaned.split('').reverse().join('');
    return cleaned === reversed;
}
```

This function `isPalindrome` checks if a given string `s` is a palindrome by first cleaning the string to remove non-alphanumeric characters and converting it to lowercase. It then compares the cleaned string with its reverse to determine if it is a palindrome.

